- Stopping: click "Stop hand control" to turn the camera off. The camera light should go off too.

The hand tracking uses MediaPipe Hand Landmarker (@mediapipe/tasks-vision@1.1.0, the current release). It loads only after someone clicks the button, so the page doesn't get slower for visitors who never use it. The video is processed in the browser and isn't uploaded anywhere.

What I tested: I ran the site in headless Chrome with a simulated camera. Clicking the button started the camera at 640×480, the hand model loaded with no errors, and stopping released the camera. The simulated camera has no hand in it, so I couldn't test hovering and pinching with a real hand. That part needs you in front of your webcam.

If it feels off, three settings at the top of the hand-control script control it:
- SMOOTH: lower makes the cursor steadier, higher makes it more responsive.
- MARGIN: lower if it's hard to reach the edges of the screen.
- PINCH_ON: raise if pinches don't register, lower if it clicks by accident.

