- Hand mix-ups: a hand in the same spot your left hand just was is treated as still your left hand, whatever label MediaPipe gives it.
- Stopping: turning still starts only when all five fingers are clearly open. It now stops only when two or more fingers are clearly curled for 5 frames in a row, like a fist or pointing. A few misread frames no longer end it.
- Tracking gaps: if tracking drops out for up to about 0.4 s, the turn holds and continues from where it was when your hand reappears.

I tested this by playing a simulated turn with each of those glitches through the hand-control code. Turning continued through all of them and stopped only when the hand closed. I can't see your real camera feed, so I haven't confirmed these were the exact causes for you. If it still stops, notice whether the status line switches back from "Turning the brain" when it happens, and tell me.
